# Normalizacion de finales de linea, dicha en el repo y no en la config de cada maquina.
#
# Sin este fichero el resultado depende de `core.autocrlf` de quien clone: un colaborador con
# autocrlf=false ve CRLF donde otro ve LF, y cualquier fichero que toque Power BI Desktop sale
# con el diff entero cambiado aunque no se haya editado ni una linea.

* text=auto

# Power BI Desktop reescribe TMDL, PBIR y sus JSON con CRLF cada vez que guarda. Fijarlo aqui
# evita que un editor que guarde LF produzca un diff de fichero completo en el siguiente
# guardado de Desktop.
*.tmdl      text eol=crlf
*.pbip      text eol=crlf
*.pbism     text eol=crlf
*.pbir      text eol=crlf
*.platform  text eol=crlf

# Los datos del laboratorio van como CSV pequenos o Enter Data. Si
# alguien trae una copia local, que git no intente normalizarla.
*.parquet   binary
*.pbix      binary
*.abf       binary
# Los scripts de shell corren dentro de contenedores Linux. Con CRLF el shebang queda como
# "#!/bin/sh" seguido de un retorno de carro y el script deja de encontrarse
# (lab/drafting/entrypoint.sh: "dsh-run: not found").
*.sh        text eol=lf

# The plugin folder is the repo root, so what reaches the plugin directory is the repo
# archive (git archive, or GitHub's zip). The raw #shared exports are input to sync_shared.py,
# not something the agent reads: they stay in the repo so every generation can be reproduced,
# and out of the archive (1.09 MB, over the 256 KiB a plugin file may weigh).
exports/*.json export-ignore
# The review PBIPs (the folders under lab/review/) are for reading the examples in Power BI;
# the agent never reads them. 929 files and about 4 MB, each with the author's thank-you page:
# they stay in the repo and in CI, which works on the checkout, and out of the archive. The
# trailing slash drops the folders themselves too, not only their files.
lab/review/*/ export-ignore
